pre_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
NOTE: mpv-dovi-vfx-git carries five extra filters that are dlopen()-based,
      not linked into the binary:

        hwup     upload CUDA/NVDEC frames to a CUDA device buffer
        vsr      NVIDIA NGX VideoSuperRes (AI upscale)
        truehdr  NVIDIA NGX TrueHDR (SDR -> HDR10)
        vfg      NVIDIA VideoFrameGeneration (frame interpolation)
        dlssnr   DLSS 5 Neural Render (NGX feature 18, via dlssnr-helper)

      They need the NVIDIA VFX SDK runtime. The loader looks for it in
      $HOME/.local/lib/vsr-player and enables the filters when it is present;
      when it is missing, mpv still runs normally and the filters just error
      out on first use.

      Required runtime pieces, none of which are hard package dependencies:
        - the proprietary NVIDIA driver (libcuda.so.1)
        - the 'cuda' package (libnvrtc.so.13, used to JIT the YUV->RGBA kernel)
        - an RTX GPU with the NGX models for VSR / TrueHDR / VFG

      The AI chain must decode through NVDEC (--hwdec=nvdec). With
      --hwdec=vulkan the frames cannot be uploaded to CUDA and hwup disables
      the whole chain.

      dlssnr is the one filter that needs a second process: the shared-memory
      server 'dlssnr-helper' must be running (~/.local/bin/dlssnr-helper start,
      and a reboot stops it). Without it the NR filter logs and fails open,
      it does not crash playback.

      The Dolby Vision P7/P8 path is unaffected and needs no extra runtime.
EOF
}

pre_upgrade() {
  if pacman -Q mpv-dovi-git >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    cat <<'EOF'
NOTE: this package replaces mpv-dovi-git: the same static libplacebo/FFmpeg
      DoVi stack, plus the NVIDIA VFX filters. mpv and libplacebo are pinned to
      the exact commits in _mpvcommit/_lpcommit in the PKGBUILD, which is why
      the version string carries a git hash. Your ~/.config/mpv/mpv.conf keeps
      working unchanged.
EOF
  fi
}
